# their frozen inputs and PCT runtime, so they add little real disk).
# HarnessVLN native PCT/SCAN/Lite3 V12 Isaac runs on gpu5070ti:
# - per-run copies of the materialized PCT runtime, native libraries plus pinned Python source (identity:
#   p2b_execution/pct_runtime_manifest.json and each run's source_env_hashes.json; rebuild with
#   p2b_execution/freeze_pct_runtime.py);
# - per-run copies of the frozen scene and map inputs (identity: p2b_execution/input_manifest.json);
# - third-person, RViz and preview videos and review frames;
# - 17 point-cloud, journal and metrics dumps over 5 MB (Dr Sun, 2026-09-16; 13 are also in
#   .pipeline/handoffs/2026-09-16_harnessvln_archive/evidence.tar.gz).
# - 2026-09-17 SCAN fix qualification: per-episode walk review videos, and report figures and video links
#   (scan_fix_qualification/report; regenerate with make_report.py). The episodes' clouds.jsonl and original
#   third-person video stay on gpu5070ti (hashes in each run's remote_only_artifacts.json, PRD D9).
# - 2026-09-17 stance-hold qualification (task 09-17-isaac-runner-stance-hold): three 60 s stand runs and
#   six scripted walk runs under isaac_runner/runs/, their side-view videos, and the review videos and figures
#   in stance_hold_qualification/. Their clouds.jsonl (31-84 MB) and the stand runs' metrics.jsonl (9.6-12 MB)
#   are local-only; every walk run's metrics.jsonl (4.2 MB), summary, setup and hash records stay tracked, and
#   the analysis JSONs regenerate from them with analyze_stance_hold.py and compare_pre_entry.py.
# Run outputs are not regenerable. Nested .gitignore files in this root cover pi/node_modules and the
# p2b_execution inputs, runtime and build sources.
